# Pairs with RAllOrNothing. Regression check for issue #4448, fixed by #4461.
# The point read path answers Indeterminate for a delegation whose coordinator
# cannot be dialled; before #4461 the snapshot read paths (SnapshotAsync,
# SnapshotWithRevisionAsync) left such a txid out of the snapshot, and
# TxDecisionView resolves an absent txid to InFlight. A multi-key receiver
# reader resolving through a snapshot therefore served a delegated tree's key
# pre-saga while the barrier had committed and a sibling tree was finalised.
# Since #4461 the snapshot carries the txid as Indeterminate, which is the
# base's single read view. This edits the read view, not an action: it is the
# answer one class of reader was given, which is exactly where the defect lived.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingSnapshotReadsUnresolvableAsInFlight
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an undiallable receiver delegation reads InFlight rather than Indeterminate, as the snapshot read paths answered it before #4461

--- FIND
    ELSE IF rdeleg[tr] THEN (IF rdial[tr] THEN "indeterminate" ELSE cdec)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the unresolvable delegation is left out, so it reads InFlight.
    ELSE IF rdeleg[tr] THEN (IF rdial[tr] THEN "inflight" ELSE cdec)
--- END
